{%- case gem_handle -%}

  {%- when 'navratana' -%}
  <div class="gem-tab gem-tab--navratana">
    <h2>What Navratna Is Not</h2>
    <b>Not a Collection of Independent Remedies</b>
    <p>Navratna is not nine separate astrological gemstones worn for nine separate purposes.</p>
    <p>Nor is it simply a jewellery design containing multiple coloured stones.</p>
    <p>Its significance comes from the relationship between the gemstones and the balance they are traditionally believed to create together.</p>
    <p>The value of Navratna lies not in any single gemstone.</p>
    <p>It lies in the harmony of all nine.</p>
   
  </div>

  {%- when 'upratnas' -%}
  <div class="gem-tab gem-tab--upratnas">
    <h2>What Upratnas Are Not</h2>
    <b>Not a Fake, Not a Compromise</b>
    <ul>
      <p>One of the most common misconceptions about Upratnas is that they are simply cheaper versions of more famous gemstones.</p>
      <p>They are not.</p>
      <p>An Upratna is not a synthetic substitute, an imitation stone, or a replica designed to resemble another gemstone. It is a genuine natural gemstone with its own geological origin, mineral composition, and traditional significance.</p>
      <p>The value of an Upratna should not be measured only by rarity or price. Many have been worn, gifted, collected, and respected for centuries in their own right.</p>
      <p>Their purpose is not to imitate another stone.</p>
      <p>Their purpose is to offer a different expression of the same tradition.</p>
    </ul>
  </div>

